//------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//   VAMPIRE quantum module
//
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//   The module supplies thermal noise with a quantum spectral density to the
//   spin dynamics, either as the open-system LLG (a spin coupled to an
//   auxiliary oscillator with a Lorentzian response) or as a coloured
//   replacement for the classical white thermal field of another integrator.
//
//   Modes
//   -----
//   sim:integrator selects the consumer, quantum:noise-type the spectrum:
//
//     llg-quantum        open-system LLG, integrated by this module. Any
//                        spectrum, including classical (the classical
//                        open-system model). Needs the material parameters
//                        quantum-lorentzian-width and
//                        quantum-lorentzian-central-frequency.
//     llg-heun           coloured spin bath added to the effective field when
//                        the spectrum is not classical; otherwise the stock
//                        integrator with sim::calculate_thermal_fields() runs
//                        untouched.
//     spin-lattice       coloured spin bath and coloured lattice (force) bath
//                        when the spectrum is not classical.
//
//   Spectra
//   -------
//   With T the reduced temperature (kB T/hbar in the bath's frequency unit)
//
//     classical          S(w) = 2T
//     quantum            S(w) = w coth(w/2T)             (with zero-point term)
//     quantum-no-zero    S(w) = w (coth(w/2T) - 1)       (without zero-point term)
//
//   All three tend to 2T for w -> 0, so a coloured bath reproduces the
//   classical white noise in that limit and the amplitudes below are fixed
//   by requiring exactly that.
//
//   Generators
//   ----------
//   on-the-fly (default): auxiliary Ornstein-Uhlenbeck modes per site and
//     component, one exact update per step. quantum uses n_bath_modes
//     Matsubara modes at 2 pi n T plus a white zero mode; quantum-no-zero
//     uses n_bath_modes log-spaced modes whose rate window is fitted once at
//     start (a grid scan against the target spectrum, see bath_log.cpp) and
//     whose amplitudes follow the temperature afterwards. Works with programs
//     that change the temperature.
//
//   pre-generated: white noise shaped in frequency space by sqrt(S(w)),
//     and for the thermostat by the Lorentzian as well, then read back with
//     linear interpolation. Generation is windowed (overlap-save, six
//     segments per transform of which four are kept). With no
//     quantum:noise-window-size the whole run is covered by one window,
//     which costs an FFT length of 6/4 of the run and a buffer of
//     3*atoms*(4/6 + 2/6)*n_coarse doubles; the module refuses above 8 GiB
//     and asks for a window size instead. The spectrum is frozen at the
//     starting temperature, so programs that change the temperature are
//     refused. The first window is generated at the first step, after the
//     random number generator has been seeded, so sim:integrator-random-seed
//     applies to it.
//
//   Amplitudes
//   ----------
//   The baths deliver unit-variance samples; the consumer's amplitude is
//   applied on output, per material:
//
//     thermostat, on-the-fly     sqrt(gamma A/S0),  A = alpha omega0^4/gamma,
//                                S0 = mu_s/(hbar gamma_e); the oscillator
//                                filters the bath
//     thermostat, pre-generated  1/sqrt(S0); the Lorentzian is in the filter
//     llg-heun                   H_th_sigma sqrt(dt hbar gamma_e/2kB)
//     spin-lattice, spin         the same, with H_th_sigma_eq during
//                                equilibration
//     spin-lattice, lattice      sqrt(eta hbar/m) in eV, ps and A, with
//                                eq_damp_lat during equilibration; the bath
//                                runs at the lattice step dt_SI in ps and
//                                the temperature scale kB/hbar in 1/ps
//
//   Coloured baths use sim:temperature. Material temperatures and
//   temperature rescaling are corrections to the classical model and stay
//   with the classical thermal field; the module says so in the log when
//   they are set.
//
//   Checkpoints hold spins, velocities and the random number generator, not
//   the bath state: a restarted coloured run begins with a cold bath and a
//   short transient.
//
//   Keywords
//   --------
//   quantum:noise-type              classical | quantum | quantum-no-zero
//   quantum:noise-generator         on-the-fly | pre-generated
//   quantum:noise-window-size       fine steps per window (0 = whole run)
//   quantum:noise-interpolation-factor  fine steps per coarse sample
//   quantum:bath-modes              modes per site (default 30)
//   quantum:bath-scan-resolution    grid points per axis of the log-bath fit
//   quantum:bath-scan-omega-points  frequency points of the log-bath fit
//   quantum:bath-scan-decades       width of the log-bath search box
//   quantum:export-noise [= file]   write the noise seen by one atom
//   quantum:export-noise-atom       which atom (default 0)
//   material:quantum-lorentzian-width              Gamma, reduced units
//   material:quantum-lorentzian-central-frequency  omega0, reduced units
//
//   Deprecated spellings, still accepted with a note in the log:
//   sim:integrator = llg-heun-quantum (llg-heun; spectrum defaults to
//   quantum), quantum:heun-noise-type, quantum:llg-method = llg-ho | llg-fft,
//   quantum:heun-export-noise[-atom], spin-lattice:noise-type,
//   spin-lattice:export-noise[-atom], and the values quantum-fft /
//   quantum-no-zero-fft for noise-type.
//
//   Files
//   -----
//   internal.hpp    types (bath_t, fft_t), shared variables, declarations
//   data.cpp        definitions and defaults
//   interface.cpp   keywords
//   initialize.cpp  mode decision, amplitudes, run length, banner, cleanup
//   bath.cpp        bath setup, temperature refresh, per-step draw; public
//                   enabled/generate/field/add_field/lattice_field
//   bath_ou.cpp     Matsubara Ornstein-Uhlenbeck generator
//   bath_log.cpp    log-spaced Ornstein-Uhlenbeck generator and its fit
//   bath_fft.cpp    pre-generated (overlap-save FFT) generator
//   export.cpp      noise export
//   llg_atom.hpp    per-atom arithmetic shared by the CPU steppers and a
//                   future GPU kernel: equations of motion, RK4 stages,
//                   one-site bath updates
//   llg.cpp         stepper dispatch, RK4 range helpers, thermostat storage
//   llg_serial.cpp  serial steppers for on-the-fly and pre-generated noise
//   llg_mpi.cpp     the same with halo swaps
//
//   References
//   ----------
//   J. Barker and G. E. W. Bauer, Phys. Rev. B 100, 140401(R) (2019)
//   https://doi.org/10.21105/joss.06263
//
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------
